  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Resolve a 2D Chamfer selection as closed loops plus joined open runs.\n- Keep each open run from end to end. Enter and leave it on the air side.\n- Emit one edge-break record for each selected run.\n- Refuse a collapsed open segment before selection deduplication.\n- Refuse an open edge with no model wall at the chamfer depth.\n- Refuse open chamfer runs when Boundary settings shape an area.\n- Keep the existing cone, diameter, flute-length, wall, gouge, and stock checks.\n- Add the unattended design record for the open-run lead law.\n\n## Earlier validation\n\n- Motion tests pin one open edge, connected edges, separate chains, a collapsed segment, and a missing model wall.\n- App tests pin one selected edge, connected edges, separate chains, no credit for an unselected edge, and Boundary settings with open runs.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test chamfer_circular`: 12 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test chamfer_open_edges`: 5 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 22 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- At head `2fbe6f2fbb33d3be8181ae6097766f2b1415c94e`, `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` passed 236 of 236 steps. The tests reported 2,539 passed and 71 ignored.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main`: 235 of 236 steps passed.\n- The failed heavy step is `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`. The same `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` failure occurs on unchanged `origin/main` and is tracked in #3085.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `graphify update` did not run because `graphify` is not on `PATH`.\n\n## Manual test\n\nA manual GUI test on `O4 Cam Plate master` selected several edges and generated only their chamfer paths. No closed loop was required.\n\n## Final fix round\n\nHead: `c1b0caaa6af2f97bdfc5b3ffae0a442d1d001cf0`.\nMerged `upstream/main` at `db3bb1f7f` into the contributor branch. Kept all contributor commits.\n\nThe four conflicts contain separate additions to operation matches. The resolution keeps both `Chamfer2D` and `WaterjetProfile` in:\n\n- `collect_job`: the exclusion from `picked_region`.\n- `collect_job`: the match for `contour_sel`.\n- `selection_geometry_impl`: the match before `join_open_runs`.\n- `selection_geometry_in`: the `contour` match.\n\nThe change keeps the existing refusal checks. The delta contains the same eight files as the original PR.\n\n## Final validation\n\nThese results apply to head `c1b0caaa6af2f97bdfc5b3ffae0a442d1d001cf0` against `upstream/main` at `db3bb1f7f`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 308 of 308 steps passed in 39 minutes.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 99 of 99 steps passed in 45.1 minutes. No step failed or stalled.\n- The heavy gate includes four expected-red controls: three for #1950 and one for #2849. Seven unreached kernel steps were skipped.\n- `cargo clippy -j 16 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `chamfer_circular`: 12 passed.\n- `chamfer_modelled_edge`: 7 passed.\n- `chamfer_open_edges`: 5 passed.\n- The quick gate also passed the touched suites, including the Waterjet coverage.\n- `app suites: example_catalog`: 39 passed and 4 ignored.\n- Adaptive catalog suite: 1 passed.\n- Edge-work catalog suite: 1 passed.\n- `golden_cl`: 34 passed.\n- `solid_law_goldens`: 7 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 of 6 steps passed in 1.4 minutes.\n\n## Pin proof\n\n- `an_open_chamfer_with_a_collapsed_segment_refuses_by_name` passed in `chamfer_circular`.\n- `an_open_chamfer_without_a_model_wall_refuses_by_name` passed in `chamfer_circular`.\n- `open_chamfer_runs_with_boundary_area_settings_refuse_by_name` passed in `chamfer_open_edges`.\n- The mutation removed `Chamfer2D` from all four resolved matches. All five `chamfer_open_edges` tests failed.\n- Restoring the exact source made all five tests pass. The tree is clean after restoration.\n- The existing refusal implementations did not change. This round did not mutate the two motion refusal implementations separately.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog and reached golden suites passed. No recorded program changed.\n\n## Final limitations\n\n- Quick and heavy gates used merged upstream `db3bb1f7f3c47cf3561a8e9534f4f2cde260cba8`, which was current when verification started.\n- Upstream moved during more than 85 minutes of verification to `940cc5d0ee8f2e5b8024bd5389aaefba5682751a`.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD upstream/main` exited 0. The latest-main merge simulation was clean and produced tree `b55781852f3feb411489e669a29cf1d1b50e7753`.\n- Checklist limitation: full validation against the newer upstream snapshot did not run. The tested head is preserved without another merge beyond the conflict fixes.\n- The manual GUI test was not repeated in this round.\n- This fix round changes no UI. Before and after screenshots do not apply.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer can now machine one or more selected open edge chains without cutting the complete edge loop.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2988\n\n",
